+name: sublingual gland ducto-acinar unit
+def: "A salivary gland ducto-acinar unit that is part of the sublingual gland, consisting predominantly of mucous acini together with their contiguous ductal segments, and associated myoepithelial cells, stromal tissue, and vasculature. This unit produces a viscous, mucin-rich saliva." [PMID:24862590, PMID:30855909]
